cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LLM-scCurator in your research, please cite this software."
title: "LLM-scCurator: Data-centric feature distillation for zero-shot cell-type annotation"
type: software
version: "0.1.4"
authors:
  - family-names: "Furudate"
    given-names: "Ken"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kenflab/LLM-scCurator"
url: "https://github.com/kenflab/LLM-scCurator"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "single-cell"
  - "spatial transcriptomics"
  - "cell-type annotation"
  - "large language models"
  - "Scanpy"
  - "Seurat"
  - "zero-shot"
  - "bioinformatics"
abstract: >
  LLM-scCurator is a Python framework for preparing marker gene lists
  for zero-shot cell-type annotation with large language models.
  It suppresses recurrent low-specificity signals and retains or
  recovers informative markers before annotation. The framework
  supports single-cell and spatial transcriptomic workflows.
  The repository includes benchmark evaluation scripts, label mappings,
  scoring configurations, and source data accompanying the revised
  manuscript, including external validation using the Human Lung
  Cell Atlas.
